{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC -- see sections.json. One /v1/users/<uid>/events window.",
    "The window parameters are start_date/end_date (YYYY-MM-DD). Passing",
    "start/end instead does NOT error: they are read as paging offsets and the",
    "reply is a cheerful {\"event\": [], \"total\": N}.",
    "  * event ids and assignment ids are DISJOINT sequences: /assignment/<event_id>",
    "    is a 403, so links must be built from the event's own assignment_id",
    "Cases here:",
    "  * type=event that is really an assignment (a teacher posting work as a",
    "    calendar entry) -- it never reaches the upcoming widget or gradebook",
    "  * the SAME item twice under two ids: teachers do create duplicates, so",
    "    deduplication keys on (title, start, section_id), not id",
    "  * an HTML-escaped title -- /v1 escapes these and it is easy to miss",
    "  * realm=school with no section_id, which must not crash the join"
  ],
